      "point": "The analyst surfaces one piece of evidence I did not explicitly weigh in round-1: there is no burn rate, headcount, or runway disclosure at all. I noted the 33x ARR multiple and flagged the vision question, but I did not address the complete absence of capital-efficiency data. At a $4M ask, the difference between a 2-person team burning $50K/month and a 15-person team burning $350K/month is not a detail — it changes the runway math and the capital efficiency story materially. This is a genuine evidentiary gap the analyst correctly identifies. I am adding it to my diligence requirements. That said, this gap does not move my verdict from invest to more_diligence: it is a disclosure absence rather than evidence of capital mismanagement, and the 80% gross margins and 4.5-month implied CAC payback already confirm the economic engine is structurally sound. The analyst's concern about the 4-month growth window I already weighed in round-1 — it is a real limitation but expected at seed.",
