      "point": "The operator wants to see the machine that produced the 120-customer, 18%-MoM result before committing. I read that result differently: organic pull at 18% per month without a disclosed, formalized GTM engine is a stronger signal than 18% growth powered by a documented sales playbook. A formalized playbook at this stage is a nice-to-have; proof that the market is actively finding the product without one is a seed-stage strength, not a gap. The commercial co-founder absence is a real concern I noted in round-1, and I agree it needs to be addressed — but 'no formal playbook' and 'product is pulling customers anyway' describe the same fact differently. I do concede the operator's point that retention must be confirmed with actual numbers rather than the implied characterization in the materials — that is a legitimate evidentiary gap the operator correctly flags, and it belongs in my diligence list.",
